{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Deferred Actor Removal.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Deferred Actor Removal.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"deferred actor removal deferred actor removal","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Deferred Actor Removal.md","fileName":"Deferred Actor Removal.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Deferred Actor Removal","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-20 23:34\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[C++ Game Engine Architecture]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["C++ Game Engine Architecture","gameprogrammingincplusplus.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Deferred Actor Removal.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Deferred Actor Removal.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"deferred actor removal deferred actor removal","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Deferred Actor Removal.md","fileName":"Deferred Actor Removal.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Deferred Actor Removal","heading":"Deferred Actor Removal","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Deferred actor removal marks an actor for deletion during an update but erases it only after the active actor iteration finishes. This prevents iterator invalidation and use-after-free errors when an actor destroys itself or another actor mid-frame.\n\nNew actors may likewise be collected in a pending list until the current traversal completes. The world then applies additions and removals at a controlled synchronization point.","tags":["baby"],"links":["C++ Game Engine Architecture","gameprogrammingincplusplus.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Deferred Actor Removal.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Deferred Actor Removal.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"deferred actor removal deferred actor removal